{"ts": 1784343700.9018404, "event": "finish", "summary": "Held the entire window. The entry was right-direction from frame 0 onward - price pushed favorable almost immediately (+24.75 by t=1m) and kept making new highs through t=24m (peak +53.5), with only a handful of sharp but shallow pullbacks (worst dip to +21 at t=26m after a fast reversal candle) that each recovered within 1-2 frames. Nothing ever threatened to go negative or showed a sustained lower-high/lower-low breakdown, so there was never a wrong-direction signal to act on - this looks like a good trade that should have been held past the window, not one needing a bail. Next time I'd watch for: a pullback that fails to reclaim the prior swing high within ~2-3 frames, or a leg-age/giveback combo where giveback stays >70% for multiple consecutive frames - those would be the earlier tells of a real reversal versus the noise dips seen here.", "exit_frame": null, "n_commits": 32}
